G5438G.def:
φυλακή, -ῆς, ἡ
(φυλάσσω) [in LXX chiefly for מִשְׁמֶרֶת and cogn. forms, also for כֶּלֶא etc. ;] 
__(a) actively, a guarding, guard, watch (Hom., Plat., Xen., al.): cogn. accusative, φυλάσσειν φυλακάς, to keep watch, Luc 2:8; 
__(b) of those who keep watch (as also Lat. custodia), a guard; pl., sentinels, a guard (Hom., al.): Actes 12:10; 
__(with) of the place where persons are kept under guard, a prison (Hdt., Thuc., al.): Matthieu 14:10, Marc 6:17, Luc 3:20, Actes 5:19, 2 Corinthiens 6:5, 1 Pierre 3:19, Apocalypse 18:2, al.; 
__(d) of the time during which guard was kept by night (Lest. vigilia; Anthol.), a watch: Matthieu 14:25 24:43, Marc 6:48, Luc 12:38

