G5442G.def:
φυλάσσω 
[in LXX chiefly and very frequently for שָׁמַר, also for נָצַר, etc. ;] 
to guard, watch; 
__(a) to guard or watch: with cogn. accusative, φυλακάς, Luc 2:8; with accusative of person(s), Actes 12:4 28:16; pass., Luc 8:29, Actes 23:35; with accusative of thing(s), Actes 22:20; 
__(b) to guard or protect: with accusative, Luc 11:21, Jean 12:25 17:12, 2 Thessaloniciens 3:3, 1 Timothée 6:20, 2 Timothée 1:12 1:14, 2 Pierre 2:5; ἑαυτὸν ἀπό, 1 Jean 5:21 (Westc., in l); metaphorically of law, precept, etc., to keep, preserve, observe: Matthieu 19:20, Luc 11:28 18:21, Jean 12:47, Actes 7:53 16:4 21:24, Romains 2:26, Galates 6:13, 1 Timothée 5:21. Mid., to be on one's guard (against), keep oneself from, beware of: with accusative, Actes 21:25, 2 Timothée 4:15; before ἀπό., Luc 12:15; ἵνα μή, 2 Pierre 3:17; as in LXX (Exode 12:17, Lévitique 18:4, al.), of laws, etc., to keep, observe: ταῦτα πάντα, Marc 10:20 (cf. δια-φυάσσω).†
SYN.: τηρέω, q.v

