G5446.def:
φυσικός, -ή, -όν 
(ψύσις), 
natural 
__(a) produced by nature, innate (Xen., Arist., al.); 
__(b) according to nature (Arist., Diod., al.): opposite to παρὰ φύσιν, Romains 1:26-27; 
__(with) governed by mere natural instinct (of. Plut., Mor., 706 A): ζῷα γεγεννημένα φ. (RV, born mere animals; Mayor, born creatures of instinct; ICC, animals born of mere nature), 2 Pierre 2:12,†

G5449.def:
φύσις, -εως, ἡ
(φύω) [in LXX: Wis.7:20 13:1 19:20 אΑ, 3Ma.3:29, 4Ma.1:20 4Mac 5:7-8 4Mac 5:25 4Mac 13:27 4Mac 15:13 4Mac 15:25 4Mac 16:3 * ;] 
nature, i.e., 
__(a) the nature (natural powers or constitution) of a person or thing: Jacques 3:7, 2 Pierre 1:4; 
τέκνα φυσει ὀργῆς, Éphésiens 2:3; 
__(b) origin, birth (Soph., Xen., al.): Romains 2:27, Galates 2:15; 
__(with) nature, i.e. the regular order or law of nature: 1 Corinthiens 11:14; dative, φύσει adverbially, by nature, Romains 2:14, Galates 4:8; παρὰ φύσιν, against nature, Romains 1:26 11:24; καρὰ φ., according to nature, naturally, Romains 11:21, 24.†

G5456G.def:
φωνή, -ῆς, ἡ, 
[in LXX chiefly and very frequently for קוֹל ;] 
a voice; 
__(a) prop., of persons, Matthieu 2:18 (LXX), al.; φ. αἴρειν (ἐπαίρειν), Luc 17:13, Actes 2:14, al.; φ. μεγάλῃ εἰπεῖν (λέγειν, φωνεῖν, etc.), Luc 8:28, Actes 7:57, Apocalypse 5:12, al.; γίνεται (ἔρχεται) φ. ἐκ τ. οὐρανῶν (ἐξ οὐρανοῦ), Marc 1:11, Luc 3:22, Jean 12:28, al. (cf. DCG, ii, 810a; Dalman, Words, 204f.); ἀκούειν φωνήν (-ῆς; see: ἀκούω), Actes 9:4, 7 al.; φ. βοῶντος, Matthieu 3:3, Marc 1:3, Luc 3:4, Jean 1:23" (LXX) ; τ. θεοῦ, Jean 5:37, Hébreux 3:7, al. By meton., 
__(α) of the speaker, βλέπειν τὴν φ., Apocalypse 1:12; 
__(β) speech, language ( Genèse 11:1, 4Ma.12:7, al.): 1 Corinthiens 14:10; 
__(b) of inanimate things: Matthieu 24:31, Jean 3:8, Actes 2:6, Apocalypse 1:15b 9:9 14:2, al. (cf. Tr., Syn., §lxxxix).

