G5457.def:
φῶς (Att.. contr. from φάος; φάω), genitive, φωτός, τό, 
[in LXX chiefly for אוֹר ;] 
light (opposite to τὸ σκότος, ἡ σκοτία): Matthieu 17:2, 5, Jean 11:9-10, 2 Corinthiens 4:6; ἡλίου, Apocalypse 22:5; of a lamp, Luc 8:16 11:33, Jean 5:35, Apocalypse 18:23; of a supernatural heavenly light, Actes 9:3 12:7 22:6, 9 22:11 26:13; hence, ἄγγελος φωτός, 2 Corinthiens 11:14; ὁ κλήρος τ. ἁγίων ἐν τ. φ., Colossiens 1:12; of the divine glory, Apocalypse 21:24; by meton., of that which gives light: of fire, Marc 14:54, Luc 22:56 (cl.; 1Ma.12:29; cf. DCG, i, 595; pl., of a lamp or torch, Actes 16:29; of heavenly bodies, Jacques 1:17. 
Metaphorical, 
__(a) of God: 1 Jean 1:5 Jn 1:7; φῶς οἰκῶν ἀπρόσιτον, 1 Timothée 6:16; 
__(b) of spiritual truth and its effects on the lives of men: Matthieu 4:16 5:16, Jean 1:4-5 3:19-21, Actes 26:18, 23, 2 Corinthiens 6:14, Éphésiens 5:13, 1 Pierre 2:9, 1 Jean 2:8; τ. φ. τ. ζωῆς, Jean 8:12; τ. ὅπλα τοῦ φ., Romains 13:12; καρπὸς τοῦ φ., Éphésiens 5:9; έν τ. φ. περιπατεῖν (εἶναι, μένειν), 1 Jean 1:7 Jn 2:9-10; υἱοὶ (τέκνα) τοῦ φ., Luc 16:8, Jean 12:36, Éphésiens 5:8, 1 Thessaloniciens 5:5; by meton., of one from whom truth shines forth: Actes 13:47 (LXX), Romains 2:19; esp. of Christ, Luc 2:32, Jean 1:7-8 12:35-36, 46; τ. φ. τ. κόσμου, Jean 8:12 9:5;τ. φ. τ. ἀληθινόν, Jean 1:9; of Christians, Matthieu 5:14, Éphésiens 5:8; 
__(with) of the spiritual under­standing: τ. φ. τὸ ἐν σοί, Matthieu 6:23, Luc 11:35; 
__(d) adverbially, of that which is open to view (opposite to ἐν τ. σκοτίᾳ): ἐν τ. φ., Matthieu 10:27, Luc 12:3.†
SYN.: see: φέγγος

G5465.def:
χαλάω, -ῶ 
[in LXX: (Jérémie 38:6) (שָׁלַח pi.), etc. ;] 
__(a) to slacken, loosen; 
__(b) to let loose, let go; 
__(with) to lower, let down: with accusative of thing(s), Marc 2:4, Luc 5:4-5, Actes 9:25 27:17, 30; with accusative of person(s) (cf. Je, l.with), pass., 2 Corinthiens 11:33.†

G5467.def:
χαλεπός, -ή, -όν 
[in LXX: Ésaïe 18:2 (יָרֵא), Wis.3:19, Sir.3:21, al. ;] 
hard; 
__(a) hard to do or deal with, difficult; 
__(b) hard to bear, painful, grievous: καιροί, 2 Timothée 3:1; 
__(with) of persons, hard to deal with, harsh, fierce, savage: Matthieu 8:28.†
